{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795040438,"nonce":"L7qvB7GHhNKS4jnEGTt1puL8wO0=","message":"Implemented opt-in semantic knowledge metadata and working examples, without project-prefixed annotations. Classes/typedefs use @:knowledge(name, version), exactly one @:identity String, selected @:fact scalars/scalar arrays, typed @:relation fields using KnowledgeRef\u003cT\u003e, and optional @:spatial(worldRelation, units) point/AABB values. Knowledge.capture/remove generate selected-field reads and schema data. Unannotated fields remain excluded. Typed embedded and dynamic JSON assets can supply knowledge, including typed string references. Direct asset-field captures retain address/content-ID provenance while excluding transport paths, URIs and credentials.\n\nKnowledge publishes owned, coalesced snapshots with namespace/source revisions, one request in flight, bounded records/batches and exact-byte retry after failure. Spatial schemas retain the selected relation and units; mismatched coordinates or schema changes reject. The portable MemoryKnowledgeSink provides relationship/AABB queries. The optional native/server KyuGraph adapter is outside the haxelib and root Cargo workspace. It creates typed tables, replaces outgoing links and persists ownership, tombstones and revision/digest watermarks with graph deltas. Stale/replayed revisions survive restart; equal revisions with different data reject. KyuGraph 0.4 scalar arrays are preserved as JSON text columns because its Cypher DDL cannot declare list columns. No dedicated spatial-index claim is made.\n\nexamples/knowledge contains annotated lore/world/NPC/progress models and decoded JSON lore. Six revisions combine lore knowledge, active player progress and nearby objects, then test movement/link changes, independent progress changes and lore deletion. The same real Haxe batches drive a parameterized KyuGraph relationship/AABB query. Duplicate/stale delivery, namespace separation, unannotated-property exclusion and persistent database restart are demonstrated. The documented hxml also compiles through isolated haxelib discovery and runs under Ash, without repository class-path shortcuts.\n\nVerification: Haxe formatter and schema/negative compile checks passed, including compiler-server edits and deterministic eval/Ash full-DCE data. Existing annotation/decoder/catalog/staging tests passed. Final Mac native checks passed Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp and CPPIA. Real Chrome pages passed Ash wasm and unthreaded/threaded Emscripten. Linux NUC passed stock HashLink 1.15, all Ash modes, hxcpp and CPPIA, with repeated HL/Ash runs, using hxn 0.3.9; Linux uses its installed nightly rather than the repo-pinned nightly. The actual native KyuGraph replay/query example passed on Mac against both published 0.4.0 and local source 4662237a43adbb776fd85918d20fa0c9714c12a9, and on Linux NUC against published 0.4.0. Installed iOS 17.5 simulator and Android arm64 emulator apps passed on Ash AOT and hxcpp, including new knowledge checks plus bundle/APK reads, process-restart persistence, shared logging and HTTP/WS/WSS. Physical devices, Safari and new Windows CI were not run.\n\nThe dynamic fixture exposed two Mac CPPIA issues: direct calls through an interface cast selected the parent receiver, and copying typed string arrays directly from raw JSON could crash. AssetLoader now uses an explicit typed streaming receiver. Knowledge data rebuilds typed relationship lists at JSON boundaries, with a retained provider-roundtrip regression. Real Ash/CPPIA HTTP/WS/WSS tests pass after the receiver fix. Emscripten fixtures enable normal heap growth for bounded-payload stress cases; SDK publication limits remain enforced independently of the application heap.\n\nRust workspace fmt/clippy/tests passed (4 remote and 6 storage integration tests). Optional adapter fmt/clippy passed. Its 447 pinned dependency notice records, upstream copyright texts, LLVM exceptions and applicable source archives are separate under adapters/kyugraph/third-party; the portable file inventory remains separate and current. Notice collection can read a matching local upstream checkout at the exact packaged VCS revision. Haxe API references were regenerated as an explicitly unreleased local preview (41 pages, 38 types), with native Rust docs too. Guides, conventions, AGENTS.md, package summaries, skill/site copies and CI checks are updated; site validation passes 15 skills/347 pages. No commit, push, release or git-bug push performed for this implementation.\n\nKeep this issue open for the broader remaining acceptance: concrete Haxe native/connected KyuGraph sink integrations and live browser/mobile graph-endpoint conformance, explicit schema migration tooling, automatic asset-address/content graph mappings and cooked-variant provenance, dedicated spatial-index validation and hierarchy/transition coverage. Current APIs provide metadata, portable publication contracts and a working optional native adapter; they do not implement a hosted service, a durable client outbox or CRDT merging. Hosted infrastructure remains in 3efcf240e5267cee2e7aae0cbc2b82cedd6a0a1bde3c7891b9f86817127071de and CRDT edits/sync in 5b44833f2874c5723b0e3b1328853ced3fd707b869431ba88d1bdcff1d58767e.","files":null}]}